im":"volume","scale":"linear","scaleNote":null,"gramsPerCup":null,"size":null,"optional":false,"aisle":"spices","pantry":true,"shop":true,"one":"fine salt"}],"steps":[{"text":"Blend the flour, milk, eggs, melted butter, sugar and salt until completely smooth, scraping down the sides once. Let the batter rest in the fridge for at least {time 30 min notimer} so the crepes are tender.","uses":[0,1,2,3,4,5]},{"text":"Heat the skillet over medium heat and brush it with a little butter. Stir the batter, which may have separated.","uses":[]},{"text":"Pour in about {qty 1/4 cup fixed} of batter while tilting and swirling the pan so it coats the bottom in a thin, even layer.","uses":[]},{"text":"Cook until the edges lift and the underside is lightly golden, {time 1 min}. Loosen with a spatula, flip and cook the second side for {time 20-30 sec}.","uses":[]},{"text":"Slide the crepe onto a plate and repeat with the rest of the batter, stacking them. Brush the pan with butter every couple of crepes. The first one is often a test; that’s normal.","uses":[]}]}